WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: ar

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:48.040
There is a war raging these days, and almost no one pays attention to it.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:50.200
It involves two of the most important countries in Europe

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:53.160
and two of the most important countries in North Africa and the Arab world!

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:54.200
Let’s dive into it.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:58.440
This is Giorgia Meloni, the prime minister of the third largest economy in Europe,

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:06.080
The largest economy on earth, with a GDP of $1.88 trillion, Italy.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:11.960
She took office less than 4 months ago, and who is currently leading the first right-wing Italian government

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:18.480
since World War II. She is in two of the most important places when it comes to perpetuating the Algerian struggle

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:20.120
and its supporters against France.

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:22.840
This was Meloni's first visit to an African country.

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:28.840
She stayed for two days only, but those two days were quite enough to ignite the anger

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:31.400
of the Élysée Palace and the French press.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.920
Why did the French get so angry?

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:37.440
Because when Giorgia first landed at the airport, she visited the shrine of the martyr,

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:43.440
the famous symbol that overlooks the capital Algiers and commemorates the Algerian revolution, the martyrs,

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.880
and the people’s struggle against the French occupation.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:51.080
She also visited the Enrico Mattei Garden, named after the founder and legendary leader of the Italian oil and gas giant Eni,

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:58.440
also one of the biggest supporters of the Algerian struggle against French colonialism in the 50s and 60s.

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:02.760
The story of his death in the crash of his airplane is surrounded by exciting theories

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:05.680
suggesting that it was an assassination and not an ordinary accident,

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:14.400
such as that of Phillipe de Vosjoli, a former agent in the French Intelligence Agency, known at the time as SDECE,

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:19.800
who said that agents from the SDECE were responsible for the fall and crash of Mattei's airplane,

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:26.600
and he died because he was about to orchestrate an Italian takeover of the French oil interests in Algeria.

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:30.360
Of course, the message of the new Italian iron woman to the French

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:36.280
was made very clear during her visits to places that annoy the French officially and effectively,

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:43.240
through a declared Italian goal boldly titled "Italy as a major center for the delivery of gas supplies from Africa

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:47.560
to Northern Europe in the future", which would mean taking Russia’s place,

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:51.120
which was supplying almost half of Europe’s gas needs,

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:57.960
and at the same time pulling the rug from under the French authority in North, Central and West Africa.

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:03.640
Evidence of that is that less than a week later, Giorgia was in another Arab capital, the Libyan Tripoli!

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:26.640
 

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:33.200
These smart, quick, and calculated Italian moves prompt us to ask some very important questions, such as:

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:38.320
What is Italy’s plan in order to remain a key player in the global natural gas markets?

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:44.000
How can Algeria mainly, but also other African countries, help it achieve this goal?

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:49.440
Will the Italian infrastructure allow transporting the quantities of gas that Europe needs?

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:54.520
What are the details of the Mattei plan announced by the Italian Prime Minister in the heart of Algeria?

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:57.720
This is a sample of the important and exciting questions that we will be discussing in today’s episode.

