00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:25.800
In order to understand how Italy ended up in Algeria,

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:31.440
I must first quickly tell you about the energy situation in Italy before the Russian-Ukrainian war.

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:34.520
Exactly a year ago, before the Russian invasion of Ukraine,

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:40.000
Russia was supplying the European Union countries with 40% of their natural gas needs,

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:44.080
and Italy was the second largest importer of Russian gas after Germany.

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:48.440
It is in general one of the largest importers and users of natural gas in all of Europe.

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:56.640
it imports 90% of its supplies of natural gas, and approximately 40% of it, or about 29 billion cubic meters,

00:05:56.640 --> 00:06:04.600
was coming from Russia. In 2021 the Italian domestic consumption of gas reached 75 billion cubic meters.

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:09.000
Gas is fully responsible for generating half of the country’s electricity

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:15.000
and it is the main energy source for Italian industries and for household heating.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:19.400
But after Putin launched his still ongoing war, Italy and other European Union countries

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:23.440
found themselves threatened with a cutoff of Russian gas supplies,

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:28.280
and indeed Russian gas supplies began to gradually decrease as the war intensified

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:32.720
and the European Union imposed all kinds of sanctions on Moscow.

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:38.240
Therefore, the logical step for the Europeans was to discuss alternatives to the Russian gas.

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:42.600
During the few months after the war, Italy had two main goals:

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:49.120
a short-term goal, which was to secure its supplies of natural gas after phasing out Russian gas,

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:56.240
and a medium-term goal, which was to plan to re-export the surplus gas it imports from Africa to Europe,

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:59.480
and thus be a gas center in the European continent.

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:05.560
Thanks to precise moves made by Eni, the Italian energy giant, and former prime minister Mario Draghi,

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:13.120
Italy has largely succeeded in achieving its short-term goal of securing the country's natural gas supplies

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:18.440
and weaning it off Russian gas. Guess who supplied the Italians with their needs of natural gas?

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:20.000
Exactly, Algeria!

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:29.040
Algeria was, at that moment, Italy's second largest gas supplier to after Russia, supplying 29% of Italy's total gas flows,

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:32.960
meaning approximately 21.2 billion cubic meters,

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:37.480
but the Italians wanted an additional 9 billion cubic meters of Algerian gas.

00:07:37.480 --> 00:07:42.600
That is why Mario Draghi led a high-level delegation a month and a half after the Russian invasion

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:49.520
to secure this agreement and convince the Algerians to sign it, and also to secure a foothold for Eni there.

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:53.800
Of course, Claudio Descalzi, CEO of Eni

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:56.680
and one of the most important Italian businessmen ever, was with him in the delegation.

00:07:56.680 --> 00:08:03.040
The visit was so successful that at the end of May, the Algerian President Abdelmadjid Tebboune reciprocated the visit

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:07.320
and traveled to Rome, and there he made a logical and understandable request to the Italians:

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:11.760
You want more gas, then you must help us raise our production capacities.

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:17.680
As a result, the two energy giants, the Italian company Eni and the Algerian state-owned Sonatrach,

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:22.360
signed an agreement to boost gas exploration and accelerate the development of existing fields,

00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:28.480
to develop green hydrogen projects in Algeria, and to lay a submarine cable from Algeria to Italy to transmit electricity.

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:38.240
They also agreed to gradually increase gas flows to reach the 9 billion meters cube required by the Italians by 2023-2024.

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:44.240
After this mutual visit, the Italian Prime Minister made frequent visits to Algeria in particular

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:49.240
and to other countries around the world in general to secure gas supplies away from Russia.

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:59.200
This effort had the greatest impact on Russia's supplies, which decreased by 40%, reaching only 10% of Italian gas imports,

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:01.960
starting from late September 2022.

00:09:01.960 --> 00:09:05.511
Italy succeeded in giving up most of the Russian gas,

00:09:05.511 --> 00:09:11.400
and compensated for it by increasing gas supplies mainly from Algeria and to a lesser extent from Egypt and Libya,

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:16.520
after Mario Draghi's effective maneuvers with the help of his right-hand in the field of energy, Claudio Descalzi.

00:09:16.520 --> 00:09:22.640
This is where Mario's role ends, kudos to him, and the role of the new iron woman, Giorgia Meloni, begins,

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:28.960
who took office after her conservative right-wing party, "Brothers of Italy," won the elections in October

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:36.240
and thus formed the new Italian government, while at the same time terrifying Europe with this victory.

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:37.480
Why?

00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:42.240
To let you understand, let me give you a little glimpse into Giorgia's background and where it comes from.

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:48.320
The Brothers of Italy party, led by Giorgia, is the main heir to the so-called "neo-fascism",

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:54.600
and the party's members are very nice people who sanctify nationalism, hold great skepticism about the European Union

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:58.920
and the usefulness of its existence, and want to renegotiate the European Union treaties.

00:09:58.920 --> 00:10:04.960
Meloni's motto in her election campaign was a populist slogan titled "Italy and the Italian people first",

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:11.080
and most of her government is formed by members of her right-wing party, and from other right-wing and conservative parties

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:17.520
such as the Lega Nord party, and the former Italian Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi's party, Forza Italia.

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:41.320
 

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:45.560
In brief, Meloni sees and prioritizes the nationalism of her country only,

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:53.080
and the first goal she started working on immediately after taking office is placing Italy in a major strategic position

00:10:53.080 --> 00:10:58.960
on the global natural gas map, while also planning to make it the next major European gas center.

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:02.320
The spearhead in achieving this goal is Algeria.

00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:10.080
Algeria is the largest exporter of gas in Africa. It produces 100 billion cubic meters of natural gas each year,

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:16.640
consuming half of it domestically and exporting the rest, and possesses one of the largest oil and gas reserves in Africa,

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:22.800
which however is a largely untapped resource due to a combination of mismanagement and lack of investment.

00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:29.800
Thus, Algeria's capabilities make it the main cornerstone of Giorgia Meloni's ambition,

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:33.520
which is why her first visit to an African country was to Algeria.

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:38.960
This was encouraged by the fact that the Italian operator Eni, the world's largest in the field of energy,

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:46.960
is considered the main foreign energy company operating on Algerian territory since 1981.

00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:54.040
That's why Giorgia chose Algeria to announce her grand plan, through which Italy will become a huge global gas hub.

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:56.200
A plan she called "Mattei plan".

00:11:56.200 --> 00:12:00.680
The plan's name, as it is clear, is named after the founder of Eni, Enrico Mattei,

00:12:00.680 --> 00:12:09.360
because it simply aims to repeat what Mattei did in the 50s and 60s, which was the core of Italy’s foreign policy at the time.

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:15.760
During this period, he supported Algeria's independence from France and confronted the major Anglo-American oil companies

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:18.480
because of their exploitation of African resources.

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:24.680
He defended the continent's utilization of its natural resources and tried to help them maximize their economic growth,

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:29.480
without of course forgetting his main priority, which was to strengthen the independence of his own country, Italy,

00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:32.800
in the field of energy by using some of Africa’s resources.

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:41.200
Speaking of, you should know that Eni company was at the time offering to the African countries mutual energy deals

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:48.520
with actually fair and mutually beneficial policies, something that was never provided by any other international parties.

00:12:48.520 --> 00:12:53.520
We now find, for example, that it offered Tunisia and Algeria an equal partnership to extract their oil

00:12:53.520 --> 00:13:00.600
in exchange for profit margins much lower than those offered by the major international oil companies to African countries.

00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:04.160
This largely explains why this man was assassinated

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:09.400
The Italian Prime Minister now wants to implement Mattei's strategy once again

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:15.840
and turn Italy into an energy bridge connecting Africa to Europe by investing in African countries

00:13:15.840 --> 00:13:19.040
with fair bilateral energy deals for all parties.

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:24.400
She described this investment approach as "non-predatory and cooperative",

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:30.360
especially with Algeria which has now replaced Russia as the largest supplier of natural gas to Italy.

00:13:30.360 --> 00:13:38.440
But does Italy have the proper natural gas infrastructure that would enable it to transport billions of cubic meters

00:13:38.440 --> 00:13:42.160
of excess from its domestic consumption gas from the south to the north?

00:13:42.160 --> 00:13:46.120
Look, Italy currently has 3 pipelines transporting natural gas

00:13:46.120 --> 00:13:53.280
The first line is the Enrico Mattei gas pipeline, also known by its more popular name, the TransMed Pipeline.

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:58.280
It starts from the municipality of “Hassi R’Mel” in the Algerian state of Laghouat, passes through Tunisia,

00:13:58.280 --> 00:14:05.000
then goes under the strait of Sicily, reaches Sicily itself in southern Italy, and then onto the Italian mainland.

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:11.840
The second line is the Greenstream pipeline. This line belongs to the Libyan West Gas Project,

00:14:11.840 --> 00:14:14.800
and starts from the Wafaa field in the Libyan city of Mellitah,

00:14:14.800 --> 00:14:20.440
passing through the Libyan northwest, then under the Mediterranean Sea, reaching Sicily in southern Italy.

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:25.760
As for the third pipeline, it is called Trans Adriatic Pipeline and is known as TAP.

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:28.680
This is part of the western European Gas Corridor project.

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:33.920
Please pay more attention here, because this pipeline consists of 3 lines that complement each other.

00:14:33.920 --> 00:14:40.988
The first line, which is called South Caucasus Pipeline, aka SCP, starts from the Shah Deniz field in the south of the Caspian Sea,

00:14:40.988 --> 00:14:46.400
the largest natural gas field in Azerbaijan, and ends on the Georgian-Turkish border.

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:53.240
Then we find the second line, which is the Trans-Anatolia gas pipeline known as TANAP,

00:14:53.240 --> 00:14:57.680
a Turkish line that starts from the city of Akhalkalaki in Georgia and crosses all of Turkey

00:14:57.680 --> 00:15:01.760
until it reaches the Greek village of Kipoi. Here is where the third line starts,

00:15:01.760 --> 00:15:06.400
the Trans Adriatic Pipeline (TAP), which goes from Greece to Albania

00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:11.440
and then under the Adriatic Sea until it reaches the San Foca region in eastern Italy.

00:15:11.440 --> 00:15:15.120
These are the 3 pipelines that currently supply Italy with natural gas,

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:23.320
but if Giorgia wants to lead Italy to become the first gas center for Europe, then these pipelines are not enough.

00:15:23.320 --> 00:15:29.520
That is why the Italians are taking two paths: the first is expanding these lines, and the second is laying new lines.

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:34.000
For example, Italy has started working on doubling the capacity of the TAP pipeline,

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:37.680
so that it can deliver 20 billion cubic meters of gas by 2027.

00:15:39.680 --> 00:15:47.680
During Giorgia's visit to Algeria, she made an agreement with the officials there to resume work on the Algeria-Sardinia-Italy

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:53.720
pipeline project known as Galsi. Construction of this line was supposed to start in 2012 in order be operative in 2014,

00:15:53.720 --> 00:16:00.040
but it stopped due to the discovery of a large amount of shipwreck from a French warship named Danton

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:05.440
from World War I, which sank between the Italian island of Sardinia and northern Algeria.

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:08.240
Therefore, the project was shelved.

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:13.800
Nowadays, Rome and Algeria have begun rebuilding the line that will extend from the Algerian field of Hassi R’Mel

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:18.000
to the north of the country, then to the island of Sardinia, reaching the Italian city of Piombino.

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:23.120
Additionally, Italy has 3 regasification plants to import liquefied gas and convert it into natural gas.

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:28.240
One in the Veneto region, a second in the Liguria region, and a third plant in the Tuscany region.

00:16:28.240 --> 00:16:38.600
The country’s 3 plants have a combined capacity to re-convert liquefied gas into natural gas of 15.25 billion cubic meters.

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:45.600
Moreover, a few months ago the operator of the Italian gas network, the state-run Snam company, bought a ship,

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:54.960
which serves as a floating gas storage and regasification unit (FSRU) and is called Golar Tundra, for $350 million.

00:16:54.960 --> 00:17:02.440
A month later, Snam bought another FSRU ship called BW Singapore for $400 million.

00:17:02.440 --> 00:17:06.720
Both ships have a capacity of 5 billion cubic meters of gas each.

00:17:06.720 --> 00:17:13.800
FSRU vessels generally refer to a type of enormous ship that stores gas and has the ability to convert it

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:19.040
from liquefied gas to natural gas, which renders them highly important units. That is why Stefano Venier,

00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:27.120
CEO of the Snam company, said that the two ships will provide 13% of the Italian domestic consumption needs for gas.

00:17:27.120 --> 00:17:33.120
By the way, domestic consumption is expected to decrease by 7% by next month,

00:17:33.120 --> 00:17:40.760
because at the beginning of last August the European countries approved a voluntary reduction in gas demand by 15%,

00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:43.920
with the possibility of exceptions according to each country's circumstances.

00:17:43.920 --> 00:17:50.440
Italy said that it will aim to reduce demand by only 7% and obtained an exemption from the European Council

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:53.040
based on its ability to store gas.

00:17:53.040 --> 00:18:01.200
By next month, Italian domestic consumption is expected to drop to 65.7 billion cubic meters per year.

00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:07.600
Since Italy's main goal for taking all these steps is to become the first gas corridor for Europe,

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:12.960
it must take care of the infrastructure that will transport the excess quantities of imported gas coming from

00:18:12.960 --> 00:18:18.560
the entry points that we mentioned a while ago to its strong industrial center located in the north of the country,

00:18:18.560 --> 00:18:22.960
as well as to the export channels that used to transport gas from Russia,

00:18:22.960 --> 00:18:26.280
passing it through some European countries before it reached Italy.

00:18:26.280 --> 00:18:32.960
That's not the case now, as we Italians will create a reverse flow of gas from our country to other European countries

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:38.760
through the Trans Austria Gas pipeline (TAG), which passes through Austria,

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:43.520
and through the Transitgas pipeline that goes through Switzerland as we see,

00:18:43.520 --> 00:18:48.440
which will in turn transport Italian gas to high-demand markets in Central and Western Europe.

00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:56.560
For that reason, Italy started investing $2.7 billion in an additional land pipeline that will run through the heart of Italy,

00:18:56.560 --> 00:19:00.280
called the Adriatic Line. What is the purpose of this land line?

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:06.440
It will increase the transportation capacity between the south and the north by about 10 billion cubic meters.

00:19:06.440 --> 00:19:12.640
However, it seems that Giorgia Meloni's ambition has no limits and will not be satisfied with all of this,

00:19:12.640 --> 00:19:17.360
as she is trying to take advantage of the critical situation the European Union is going through in the field of energy,

00:19:17.360 --> 00:19:22.600
in order to gain its financial and political support to achieve the Italian ambition in the region...

00:19:22.600 --> 00:19:25.880
How? Through the REPowerEU plan..

00:19:25.880 --> 00:19:30.080
This is a very huge plan developed by the European Commission in May 2022

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:36.800
to make the European Union independent of Russian fossil fuels by 2027,

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:42.400
and of course with huge sums allocated to accelerating the European Union’s diversification of natural gas supply sources...

00:19:42.400 --> 00:19:48.760
The plan will be supported by $263.5 billion in loans and grants.

00:19:48.760 --> 00:19:55.480
Of course, the European Union is now excited about any projects that will make it dispense with anything coming from Russia.

00:19:55.480 --> 00:20:01.160
That is why, on February 6, Giorgia and some of her government's ministers met with the heads of

00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:08.240
major Italian energy companies, such as the CEOs of energy giant Eni, of Enel, the Italian distributor of electricity and gas,

00:20:08.240 --> 00:20:14.120
of the Italian gas network operator Snam, and of the Italian transmission system operator Terna.

00:20:14.120 --> 00:20:21.120
After the meeting, she explicitly stated that she would use the EU funds of the REPowerEU plan

00:20:21.120 --> 00:20:27.360
to completely wean Italy from Russian gas and turn the country into an energy hub for the EU.

00:20:27.360 --> 00:20:29.360
 

00:20:45.320 --> 00:20:49.080
Therefore, considering the amount of domestic consumption after the expected decrease,

00:20:49.080 --> 00:20:54.080
the solid infrastructure that Italy owns and has begun to expand and develop,

00:20:54.080 --> 00:20:59.800
the additional quantities that Eni contracted with the Algerian company Sonatrach,

00:20:59.800 --> 00:21:07.160
the increase in imports of natural gas from Azerbaijan and liquefied gas from Egypt, Angola, the Republic of the Congo,

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:13.120
Nigeria and Mozambique, not to mention Eni's new investments in Libya and other countries,

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:16.720
which will likely bear fruit within the next 3 years,

00:21:16.720 --> 00:21:23.080
Italy will become a major exporter of natural gas to northern European countries.

00:21:23.080 --> 00:21:30.080
Thus, its strategy has succeeded, and it achieved its ambitions to become the main gas corridor for Europe,

00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:34.040
which will help it in the future to increase its weight within the European Union,

00:21:34.040 --> 00:21:40.480
and will enhance its influence in the Mediterranean region, because the country will play a major role in the energy security

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:44.640
of the European Union on one hand and will serve as the largest natural gas customer for the Mediterranean countries

00:21:44.640 --> 00:21:46.160
and Africa on the other hand.

